ash bottle stands tall and upright, casting a sharp, realistic shadow, with a large dollop of its rich, cloud-like microfoam resting beside it. The visual hero is the soothing, non-stripping microfoam texture. The short on-image headline is 'Fight acne. Keep your barrier.' The call to action is 'See the difference'. To keep the ad on-brand, maintain a high-contrast editorial look using midnight black text, Jost typography, sharp lines, clean margins, and use the review teal color to highlight the key benefit tag.\",\"prompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Ground this ad in the Before-After-Bridge framework to speak to customers dealing with irritation from active serums. The visual layout is a premium, editorial lifestyle flat-lay on a smooth, solid white surface. On the left, a generic chemical dropper bottle lies knocked over, symbolizing past skin irritation. On the right, the premium, cylindrical sniQue foam face wash bottle stands tall and upright, casting a sharp, realistic shadow, with a large dollop of its rich, cloud-like microfoam resting beside it. The visual hero is the soothing, non-stripping microfoam texture. The short on-image headline is 'Fight acne. Keep your barrier.' The call to action is 'See the difference'. To keep the ad on-brand, maintain a high-contrast editorial look using midnight black text, Jost typography, sharp lines, clean margins, and use the review teal color to highlight the key benefit tag.\\n\\nProduct appearance: This skincare product set consists of a 150 mL cylindrical foaming face wash bottle and its matching tall, rectangular cardboard outer box, both featuring a clean, minimalist white-and-light-green color palette. The bottle is made of smooth white plastic, capped with a large white foaming pump dispenser nozzle and covered by a clear, translucent cylindrical plastic cap. The bottle's main body is wrapped in a matte white label with a solid light green band at the base, matching the graphics on the rectangular box. On 