e details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nThe final attached image is the official brand logo. Add it once, subtly, in clean negative space; keep it exact, legible, and uncropped.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"source\":\"campaign-creatives\",\"language\":\"English\",\"lastError\":null,\"imageModel\":\"openai/gpt-image-2:100\",\"hasNSFWRisk\":false,\"imagePrompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Ground this ad in the Feature-Benefit-Difference framework to target the ingredient-conscious skincare lover who is wary of harsh acne treatments. The visual layout is a stark, minimalist split-screen split down the middle with a sharp line. On the left, on a dull, dry background, sits a generic clinical bottle labeled 'Ordinary 2% BHA' with text highlighting 'Stripped Barrier and Redness'. On the right, on a refreshing cool gray background, sits the pristine sniQue white-and-light-green foaming face wash bottle, pumping a dense, pillowy cloud of white foam, highlighting 'pH-Balanced BHA + Succinic Acid + Soothing Allantoin'. The visual hero is the product's ge