light green lowercase font. At the very bottom, set inside the light green band, a rounded-corner rectangular block contains the text \\\"Salicylic Acid (BHA) + Succinic Acid + Multi-fruit anti-acne complex + Allantoin\\\" in small black sans-serif font. The side panels of the box and back of the bottle display detailed product information, featuring light green section headers such as \\\"Ingredients\\\", \\\"Directions For Use\\\", and \\\"Warnings\\\" followed by dense black text detailing chemical and botanical components, application steps, and safety precautions.\\n\\nUse the product appearance text only as a private visual reference for accurately drawing the product. Do not print, quote, paraphrase, label, or turn any of that description into ad copy. Treat orientation-specific details carefully: show front-only details only when the product front is visible; if the brief shows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nThe final attached image is the official brand logo. Add it once, subtly, in clean negative space; keep it exact, legible, and uncropped.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"status\":\"generating\",\"createdBy\":\"f5dfb377-dac7-46a6-aea3-a4e04cb45e54\",\"metadata\":{\"brief\":\"Ground this ad in the Before-After-Bridge framework to speak to customers dealing with irritation from active serums. The visual layout is a premium, editorial lifestyle flat-lay on a smooth, solid white surface. On the left, a generic chemical dropper bottle lies knocked over, symbolizing past skin irritation. On the right, the premium, cylindrical sniQue foam face wash bottle stands tall and upright, casting a sharp, realistic shadow, with a large dollop of its rich, cloud-like microfoam resting beside it. The visual hero is the soothing, non-stripping microfoam texture. The short on-image headline is 'Fight acne. Keep your barrier.' The call to action is 'See the difference'. To keep the ad on-brand, maintain a high-contrast editorial look using midnight black text, Jost typography, sharp lines, clean margins, and use the review teal color to highlight the key benefit tag.\",\"prompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Ground this ad in the Before-After-Bridge framework to speak to customers dealing with irritation from active serums. The visual layout is a premium, editorial lifestyle flat-lay on a smooth, solid white surface. On the left, a generic chemical dropper bottle lies knocked over, symbolizing past skin irritation. On the right, the premium, cylindrical sniQue foam face wash bottle stands tall and upright, casting a sharp, realistic shadow, with a large dollop of its rich, cloud-like microfoam resting beside it. The visual hero is the soothing, non-stripping microfoam texture. The short on-image headline is 'Fight acne. Keep your barrier.' The call to action is 'See the difference'. To keep the ad on-brand, maintain a high-contrast editorial look using midnight black text, Jost typography, sharp lines, clean margins, and use the review teal color to highlight th