dollop of its rich, cloud-like microfoam resting beside it. The visual hero is the soothing, non-stripping microfoam texture. The short on-image headline is 'Fight acne. Keep your barrier.' The call to action is 'See the difference'. To keep the ad on-brand, maintain a high-contrast editorial look using midnight black text, Jost typography, sharp lines, clean margins, and use the review teal color to highlight the key benefit tag.\\n\\nProduct appearance: This skincare product set consists of a 150 mL cylindrical foaming face wash bottle and its matching tall, rectangular cardboard outer box, both featuring a clean, minimalist white-and-light-green color palette. The bottle is made of smooth white plastic, capped with a large white foaming pump dispenser nozzle and covered by a clear, translucent cylindrical plastic cap. The bottle's main body is wrapped in a matte white label with a solid light green band at the base, matching the graphics on the rectangular box. On the front of both the bottle and the box, the upper left side displays bold, black sans-serif text reading \\\"Anti-Acne\\\", \\\"Foam Face\\\", and \\\"Wash\\\", followed by the description \\\"Foam That Fights Acne – Gently & Effectively\\\" and a list of benefits (\\\"Clear Skin\\\", \\\"Zero Oil\\\", \\\"Gentle Foam Purity\\\") separated by a thin, horizontal green line. The brand name \\\"sniQue\\\" is printed vertically on the right in a large, stylized, rounded light green lowercase font. At the very bottom, set inside the light green band, a rounded-corner rectangular block contains the text \\\"Salicylic Acid (BHA) + Succinic Acid + Multi-fruit anti-acne complex + Allantoin\\\" in small black sans-serif font. The side panels of the box and back of the bottle display detailed product information, featuring light green section headers such as \\\"Ingredients\\\", \\\"Directions For Use\\\", and \\\"Warnings\\\" followed by dense black text detailing chemical and botanical components, application 